@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About this Application";
}

<h1 class="h3 mb-3">About this Application</h1>

<p class="text-muted">
    This is a take-home assignment submission for a Senior Full-Stack
    .NET Modernization Developer position. It is a self-contained demo
    application; no real personal data is collected, transmitted, or
    stored.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Stack</h2>
<ul>
    <li>ASP.NET Core MVC (.NET 8) with Razor views</li>
    <li>Entity Framework Core with the SQLite provider</li>
    <li>Bootstrap 5 for layout, Chart.js for the dashboard</li>
    <li>xUnit + FluentAssertions for the test suite</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Data handling</h2>
<p>
    The application uses a local SQLite database (<code>Data/providers.db</code>)
    seeded with synthetic provider records. <strong>No data leaves the local
    machine.</strong> Soft-deleted rows remain in the database for audit
    purposes and can be inspected on the
    <a asp-controller="Providers" asp-action="Deleted">Audit page</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="h5 mt-4">Source</h2>
<p>
    See the project <code>README.md</code> for architecture, soft-delete
    design rationale, run instructions, and trade-offs.
</p>
